--- /dev/null
+++ b/research.md
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+# Live compatibility research
+
+Accessed 2026-08-14 with genuine network requests before the architecture was finalized.
+
+- “VMware Cloud Foundation 9.1 Frequently Asked Questions,” Broadcom — https://www.vmware.com/docs/vmware-cloud-foundation-9-1-general-faqs — established the supported vSphere 8.0 Update 3 and NSX 4.2 workload-domain import combination and the use of VCF Operations to add an existing vCenter to an existing fleet.
+- “Product Interoperability Matrix — Upgrade Path,” Broadcom — https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Upgrade — cross-checked the pinned direct upgrade paths from vCenter, ESXi, and vSAN 8.0 U2 to 8.0 U3 and from NSX 4.1 to 4.2.
+- “Update Sequence for VMware vSphere 8.0 and Compatible VMware Products,” Broadcom KB 308161 — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/308161/update-sequence-for-vmware-vsphere-80-an.html — informed the candidate-estate order: NSX before vCenter, vCenter before ESXi, and the vSAN on-disk update after the hosts.
+- “Importing an Existing vCenter to Create a Workload Domain in VMware Cloud Foundation,” Broadcom KB 441529 — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/441529/importing-an-existing-vcenter-to-create.html — informed the final VCF Operations import step and its gate requiring automated prechecks and critical findings to be resolved before proceeding.
+- “Could not retrieve binary for component during 'Deploy and Validate' in VCF 9.1,” Broadcom KB 436258 — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/436258/could-not-retrieve-binary-for-component.html — cross-checked the 9.1 SDDC Manager, vCenter, and NSX BOM builds used by the pinned greenfield design.
+- “Build numbers and versions of VMware ESXi/ESX,” Broadcom KB 316595 — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/316595/build-numbers-and-versions-of-vmware-esx.html — cross-checked ESX build 25370933 for 9.1.0.0 and the decision to use that integrated ESX/vSAN build rather than the vCenter build.
